# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Files that must never reach version control.
#
# This project holds NO API KEY — it never calls a hosted model, so there is
# no secret to leak. The .env line is kept anyway: the habit is worth keeping,
# and anyone who copies this file into a project that DOES hold a key should
# find the protection already in place.
#
# A key committed to a repository is a leaked key even if you delete it in a
# later commit, because the old commit still contains it.
#
# (The canary "secrets" this lab plants are generated fresh for every run and
# guard nothing, so the results files that record them are safe to commit.)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Local configuration — never commit these
.env
.env.local

# The generated shop database. `npm run seed` rebuilds it, deterministically,
# from scripts/seed.ts — so the generator is the source and the .db is output.
# Committing it would mean every seed change produces an unreadable binary
# diff, and the copy in git could drift from what the script makes.
# data/schema.sql IS committed: it is the readable teaching copy.
data/*.db
data/*.db-journal
data/*.db-wal
data/*.db-shm

# The arena writes results atomically: a temp file beside the real one,
# then a rename. A crash between the two leaves the temp file behind.
docs/*.tmp

# Installed packages — restore with `npm install` instead
node_modules/

# Compiled output — regenerate with `npm run build`
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# The browser half compiles in place, so its output sits in public/ next to
# the source. Generated, not written by hand — regenerate with
# `npm run build:client`.
public/**/*.js
public/**/*.js.map

# shared/ holds types only, so it compiles to an empty module — but the
# client build still emits one next to the source, same as public/.
shared/*.js
shared/*.js.map

# Claude Code
#
# CLAUDE.md IS committed — it is project guidance and belongs in the repo.
# These are the per-developer bits that should not be:
#   settings.local.json  one person's approved-tool choices
#   .claude/*            local session state, scratch files, logs
.claude/
.claude/settings.local.json

# Editor and OS clutter
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
